Part of #58.

## Wayfinder slice

Implement the serial client-transport phase (S9a through S9d) from `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-27-retrieval-evidence-mechanical-port.md`.

Predecessor [Implement consolidated HTTP accepted-operation authority and secure v2 transport](https://github.com/Khamel83/argus/issues/97) is terminal on `main` at `a4df7d25618674d976a29c3f0865c5f7bca5bf19`.

## Scope

- fail-closed HTTP capability negotiation with a bounded origin/deployment-scoped cache and zero speculative or fallback execution POSTs;
- exact MCP protocol, method, media, body, notification, and principal-owned session behavior, including secured legacy SSE without changing its wire shape;
- explicit versioned MCP tools with frozen v1 contracts, exact v2 structured content and schemas, bounded streaming responses, and independently validated immutable release descriptors;
- CLI contract negotiation with exact stdout, stderr, exit, streaming-bound, and legacy-selection behavior;
- architecture boundaries proving MCP and CLI are authenticated HTTP-only callers with no broker, extractor, cache, readiness, or persistence authority.

## Required evidence

- advertised-v2, proven-legacy, malformed/unavailable discovery, cache expiry/origin/deployment separation, and no ambiguous retry tests;
- MCP protocol-version, method, media, 4 MiB request bound, 11 MiB response bound, notification, session concurrency/capacity/expiry/ownership, and secured legacy SSE tests;
- frozen v1 MCP tool goldens plus exact v2 input/output schemas, structured content, error layers, and startup manifest validation in independent HTTP and MCP processes;
- CLI v2 preference, proven legacy selection, no fallback POST, exact JSON stdout, diagnostic stderr, canonical exit codes, and unchanged Click usage behavior;
- full hermetic suite, changed-file Ruff, diff checks, production-config CI, PostgreSQL CI, image canaries, and bounded independent review.

## Compatibility and rollback boundary

- existing MCP tool names, schemas, text, legacy SSE shape, and legacy CLI/server selection remain available;
- v2 negotiation fails closed when discovery is absent, malformed, ambiguous, or mismatched;
- reverting S9a leaves the resolver unused; reverting S9b removes only new session/security machinery; reverting S9c removes explicit `*_v2` tools; reverting S9d leaves legacy CLI selection;
- production activation, live provider calls, paid spend, homelab mutation, secret changes, deployment, and client promotion are not authorized.

The implementation PR must use `Closes #<this issue>` and target current `main`.

