## Wayfinder slice

Implement the consolidated HTTP-authority phase (S7 + S8) from `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-27-retrieval-evidence-mechanical-port.md`.

Parent: #58. Predecessor #94 is terminal on `main` at `e43e4a01b21cd5bc7631ca1a9b35bff585b0081f`.

## Scope

- one `AcceptedOperationService` executes retrieval/extraction exactly once and supplies frozen legacy presenters plus additive version-2 presenters;
- every valid frozen fixture and all fail-closed mutations replay through the production S1/S3/S4/S5/S6 path;
- legacy HTTP/Python/CLI/MCP byte and exception semantics remain frozen while all semantic authority moves behind the accepted-operation service;
- `/api/v2/*` uses an exact canonical outcome/status/envelope contract with matching request IDs and bounded RFC 9457 errors;
- pre-execution Host, Origin, authentication, body, media, session, rate, and principal ownership checks reject before execution or persistence;
- capabilities and the immutable release manifest advertise only fully registered contracts;
- architecture tests forbid secondary execution, outcome, cache, readiness, or persistence authority outside the service.

## Required evidence

- exhaustive canonical outcome and framework-edge tests;
- early transport-security rejection with no provider, extractor, cache, session, or persistence work;
- frozen v1 parity and exactly one operation for every v1/v2 presenter;
- authenticated principal ownership and bounded retrieval sessions;
- independent process/startup manifest validation;
- full hermetic suite, Ruff, diff checks, production-config CI, PostgreSQL CI, and image canaries;
- one bounded independent review and confirmation as specified by the plan.

## Compatibility and rollback boundary

- `ARGUS_ACCEPTED_OPERATION_AUTHORITY` defaults to `legacy`;
- v1 remains available and byte-compatible;
- v2 is additive and unready while evidence authority registration is disabled;
- transport security may tighten unsafe request acceptance and must land as a separately revertible commit;
- production activation, migration execution, live provider calls, paid spend, homelab mutation, secrets, deployment, and promotion are not authorized.

The implementation PR must use `Closes #<this issue>` and target current `main`.

