## Summary

Implements S6 accepted retrieval, durable evidence, immutable cache
publication, and the recovery/CI corrections required by the finalized
Wayfinder plan.

This PR is intentionally opened against `main` as a draft so GitHub runs the
exact PostgreSQL CI at the S6 head and produces the canonical schema-0009
artifact. It includes the still-unmerged S2-S5 stack and **must not merge**
before PRs #87, #89, #91, and #93 merge in order.

## S6 behavior

- deterministic accepted-retrieval orchestration;
- durable evidence and accounting before acknowledgment;
- immutable cache publication with origin lineage;
- bounded single-flight and visible failure outcomes;
- additive migration `0009_retrieval_evidence`.

## Recovery correction

- registers schema head 0009 in runtime health and recovery compatibility;
- inventories all twelve retrieval-evidence tables;
- routes 0009 to `argus_schema_0009.json`;
- makes schema generation require an explicit registered head;
- adds non-writing `--check` behavior;
- runs the complete recovery test file in the PostgreSQL job;
- bootstraps and uploads the canonical 0009 manifest for a follow-up checked-in
  commit.

## Verification

- TDD red: three focused tests failed for missing 0009 registration and
  generator targeting/check behavior;
- TDD green: 3 passed;
- recovery/status: 126 passed, 4 PostgreSQL-only skips;
- full hermetic suite: 1,758 passed, 43 skipped;
- Ruff: clean;
- `git diff --check`: clean.

No Docker, PostgreSQL, or Argus runtime was started on the Mac. No homelab
mutation, deployment, secrets, paid calls, or destructive action occurred.

Closes #94

