## What changed

- replaces the remaining one-PR-per-micro-slice sequence with six bounded,
  closure-driven phases;
- requires every Wayfinder implementation and operational issue to reach an
  explicit terminal state;
- adds the missing schema-head 0009 recovery, manifest, and PostgreSQL CI work
  to S6;
- recognizes that pushes to `main` submit a protected production promotion and
  keeps every intermediate promotion unapproved;
- uses the existing immutable-promotion plan as the sole deployment authority;
- requires a rollback image proven compatible with schema head 0009;
- names the four successor implementation issues and the close evidence for
  #41, #42, #44, and #58;
- bounds independent review and competitive-inconclusive loops without
  assigning research or grading to the owner.

## Why

Gemini 3.6 Flash (High) found that S7-S9 was over-sliced. Claude Opus 5 then
found direct completion blockers in the current stack: 0009 is not accepted by
the recovery/health compatibility set, the manifest generator targets the
0007 alias, stacked PostgreSQL assertions are stale, and a `main` push already
submits a production promotion. The revised plan incorporates the
evidence-backed findings and rejects speculative additions.

## Validation

- exact Gemini 3.6 Flash (High) smoke test and adversarial plan review;
- exact Claude Opus 5 smoke test and final adversarial review;
- direct source verification of 0009 recovery compatibility, manifest
  generation, PostgreSQL CI selection, runtime health, and the immutable
  promotion workflow;
- live read-only verification that GitHub's `production` environment currently
  requires reviewer `Khamel83`;
- live issue/PR inventory refreshed;
- `git diff --check`.

## Impact

Documentation and execution policy only. This PR does not merge implementation
code, run Argus locally, mutate the homelab, deploy, spend provider credits, or
change secrets.
